{"name":"Savannah Sun","hex":"#ffb989","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"savannah","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of savanna."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/savannah"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"Savanna","blocks":[{"text":"A savanna or savannah is a mixed woodland-grassland biome and ecosystem characterised by the trees being sufficiently widely spaced so that the canopy does not close. The open canopy allows sufficient light to reach the ground to support an unbroken herbaceous layer consisting primarily of grasses. Four savanna forms exist; savanna woodland, where trees and shrubs form a light canopy; tree savanna, with scattered trees and shrubs; shrub savanna, with distributed shrubs; and grass savanna, where trees and shrubs are mostly nonexistent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Tarangire-Natpark800600.jpg/330px-Tarangire-Natpark800600.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savanna","wikidata":"Q42320"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun","wikidata":"Q525"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg/500px-Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg/1280px-Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg/500px-Savanna_Grasslands_%28199168845%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A grass savanna at Kruger National Park in South Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASavanna_Grasslands_(199168845).jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Australian_savanna.jpg/330px-Australian_savanna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Australian_savanna.jpg/330px-Australian_savanna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A savanna woodland in Northern Australia demonstrating the regular tree spacing characteristic of some savannas","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAustralian_savanna.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Bushfire_Australia.jpg/500px-Bushfire_Australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Bushfire_Australia.jpg/1280px-Bushfire_Australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Bushfire_Australia.jpg/500px-Bushfire_Australia.jpg?utm